%[text] %[text:anchor:T_24239890] # Applied Ordinary Differential Equations
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"Table of Contents"}
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_E8C62B23] ## Scripts
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_528c] ### [Classification.m](file:./Scripts/Classification.m)
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[173,541,563],"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] | <p align="center">![Derivatives Graph](text:image:7cb5)</p> | <p>**In this script, students will...**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} identify independent and dependent variables in differential equations</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} distinguish between ordinary and partial differential equations</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} classify differential equations by order, linearity, and homogeneity</p><p></p> | <p>**Academic disciplines**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Mathematics</p><p></p> |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- |
%[text:table]
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_6dcc] ### [SeparationOfVariables.m](file:./Scripts/SeparationOfVariables.m)
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[173,541,563],"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] | <p align="center">![Population Growth](text:image:9181)</p> | <p>**In this script, students will...**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} determine whether ordinary differential equations are separable</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} solve first-order ordinary differential equations analytically using separation of variables </p><p></p> | <p>**Applications**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Logistic population growth model</p><p></p><p>**Academic disciplines**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Mathematics</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Biology</p><p></p> |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- |
%[text:table]
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_4fc5] ### [IntegratingFactors.m](file:./Scripts/IntegratingFactors.m)
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[173,541,563],"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] | <p align="center">![Chemical Concentration](text:image:3ad7)</p> | <p>**In this script, students will...**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} find integrating factors of linear, first-order ordinary differential equations</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} solve equations analytically by multiplying by integrating factors</p><p></p> | <p>**Applications**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Chemical concentration</p><p></p><p>**Academic disciplines**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Mathematics</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Chemistry</p><p></p> |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- |
%[text:table]
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_1d20] ### [CharacteristicEquations.m](file:.\\Scripts\\CharacteristicEquations.m)
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[173,541,563],"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] | <p align="center">![Circuit](text:image:1a14)</p> | <p>**In this script, students will...**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} find characteristic equations of linear, second-order ordinary differential equations</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} use the roots of characteristic equations to solve homogeneous equations analytically</p><p></p> | <p>**Applications**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} RLC Circuits</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Mass-spring-damper</p><p></p><p>**Academic disciplines**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Mathematics</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Engineering</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Physics</p><p></p> |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- |
%[text:table]
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_59d0] ### [UndeterminedCoefficients.m](file:.\\Scripts\\UndeterminedCoefficients.m)
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[173,541,563],"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] | <p align="center">![Chemical Bonds](text:image:201b)</p> | <p>**In this script, students will...**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} solve linear, second-order, nonhomogeneous ordinary differential equations analytically using the method of undetermined coefficients</p><p></p> | <p>**Applications**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Pendulum motion</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Chemical bonds</p><p></p><p>**Academic disciplines**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Mathematics</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Physics</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Chemistry</p><p></p> |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- |
%[text:table]
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_6a41] ### [SystemsOfODEs.m](file:./Scripts/SystemsOfODEs.m) 
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[173,541,563],"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] | <p align="center">![Earthquake](text:image:5531)</p> | <p>**In this script, students will...**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} write systems of linear, homogeneous, first-order differential equations in matrix form</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} find eigenvalues and eigenvectors of these matrices</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} solve systems of ODEs analytically using these eigenvalues and eigenvectors</p><p></p> | <p>**Applications**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} SIR model of epidemiology</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Earthquake effects on buildings</p><p></p><p>**Academic disciplines**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Mathematics</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Biology</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Engineering</p><p></p> |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- |
%[text:table]
%[text] ### Additional Script
%[text] [CheckYourWork.m](file:.\\Scripts\\CheckYourWork.m) is a code visible introduction to using the symbolic computation capabilities of the Symbolic Toolbox to check your work while solving differential equations.
